# CQ 03: Which special kinds of control does a case use?
#
# Below the open and closed loop the standard names further kinds: sampling
# control 351-47-20, cascade control 351-47-25, adaptive, fuzzy, robust,
# model-based and rule-based control among them. They say how a control works
# rather than whether its path returns.
#
# Asked of the case rather than of the class hierarchy. Listing the kinds the
# pattern knows would answer the same whichever model is loaded; reporting the
# ones a case uses says what this control is.
#
# The genus is reported alongside, since every special kind sits under the open
# or the closed loop and the answer is only readable against that: a sampling
# control is a closed loop that acts at intervals rather than continuously.
PREFIX iec60050:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?control ?specialKind ?genus
WHERE {
  ?control a ?specialKind .
  ?specialKind rdfs:subClassOf+ iec60050:Control ; rdfs:subClassOf ?genus .
  FILTER(?specialKind NOT IN (iec60050:OpenLoopControl, iec60050:ClosedLoopControl))
  FILTER(isIRI(?genus))
} ORDER BY ?control ?specialKind
